        "source_url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/11830761/",
        "review_date": "",
        "detail_label": "Technical detail",
        "detail": "<p>The compound is β-phenyl-γ-aminobutyric acid. The phenyl group is commonly described as helping it reach the brain more readily than GABA itself. HCl and FAA differ in solubility and handling, not in a proven milligram-for-milligram customer effect.</p>",
        "fallback_product": "phenibut-250mg-capsules",
        "image_alt": "Nootropix Phenibut HCl 250 mg capsules"
